[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says "one issue, one fix queued". The reports say otherwise. The desk
merged them on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and
the same subjects cover three different causes. A parser fix will close only the first.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

1. **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, so tenants that write the day
   first get dates flipped. Ticket: [issue 1](https://github.com/ghostxxpol/what-it-shows-4471/issues/1).
2. **`hint`**: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at day-first tenants
   type what the hint says and the form reads it their way. The fix is the hint on the form, not
   the parser. Ticket: [issue 2](https://github.com/ghostxxpol/what-it-shows-4471/issues/2).
3. **`shift`**: five reports where the date is off by one day, not swapped (a June that is always
   a day off, an invite sent before the booking, Lisbon and Toronto getting different days). It
   looks like time zones. That is a guess from five reports, so an engineer has to confirm it.
   Ticket: [issue 3](https://github.com/ghostxxpol/what-it-shows-4471/issues/3).

<Callout kind="warn">
The intake tag is a guess made from the reporter's browser. It does not decide the problem. The
tenant does: its locale, and the booking form it runs.
</Callout>

## How the reports were placed

- One id, one report: the export repeats some rows, so each id is counted once.
- A report is `parser` or `hint` from its tenant, as `causes.ts` computes it. A `form` report from
  a booking-v3 tenant is `hint`. The rest are `parser`.
- The five reports in the desk note `oneDayMove` are `shift`. The older
  [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) counts them under `parser`.

## What to change

- Split #4471 into the three tickets above.
- Write a new decision record that replaces 0001: merge on cause, not on subject. Do not edit 0001.

